Subject: [PATCH] SecurityScopedFileEngineHandler: check sandbox and bundle paths before realpath()

In a sandboxed app (always on iOS) the handler is asked about every QFile,
QFileInfo, QDir and QSettings path. create() resolved the canonical path with
realpath() first and only then returned nullptr for paths inside the sandbox
container or the app bundle, which is nearly every path an app touches.
realpath() costs several file system calls per path component, which made it
roughly half of the main-thread time of Rebelle's iOS launch.

Check the cleaned absolute path against the two roots first and return early.
The canonical-path checks stay for paths that only resolve into the roots
through symlinks. A symlink inside the container that points at a bookmarked
location outside it is no longer looked up.

--- a/src/corelib/platform/darwin/qdarwinsecurityscopedfileengine.mm	2026-10-30 13:27:45
+++ b/src/corelib/platform/darwin/qdarwinsecurityscopedfileengine.mm	2026-10-30 13:27:45
@@ -358,6 +358,20 @@
                                  << engine.get() << "for" << fileName;
             return engine;
         }
+    }
+
+    static const QString sandboxRoot = QString::fromNSString(NSHomeDirectory());
+    static const QString bundleRoot = QString::fromNSString(NSBundle.mainBundle.bundlePath);
+
+    // Files inside the sandbox container or the application's own bundle can
+    // always be accessed directly. Check the absolute path first, because
+    // resolving the canonical path below costs several file system calls per
+    // path component, and nearly every file an app opens is in one of these.
+    {
+        const QString absolutePath = QDir::cleanPath(
+            QFileSystemEngine::absoluteName(fileSystemEntry).filePath());
+        if (absolutePath.startsWith(sandboxRoot) || absolutePath.startsWith(bundleRoot))
+            return nullptr;
     }
 
     // We're mapping the file name to existing bookmarks below, so make sure
@@ -386,12 +400,10 @@
     QString filePath = QDir::cleanPath(canonicalEntry.filePath());
 
     // Files inside the sandbox container can always be accessed directly
-    static const QString sandboxRoot = QString::fromNSString(NSHomeDirectory());
     if (filePath.startsWith(sandboxRoot))
         return nullptr;
 
     // The same applies to files inside the application's own bundle
-    static const QString bundleRoot = QString::fromNSString(NSBundle.mainBundle.bundlePath);
     if (filePath.startsWith(bundleRoot))
         return nullptr;
 
